Step 2 — Think about the state

                      Unlike Word Search, we don't need:     row + col + wordIndex
                      
                      Instead, the fundamental recursive state is:      row
                      
                      The board configuration is the mutable state being built.

              Now the important question is:              
                          What information must we maintain so that checking whether (row, col) is safe is efficient?
              
              A queen is unsafe if another queen already occupies:
                                                                  same column
                                                                  same \ diagonal
                                                                  same / diagonal

              We therefore need to track three sets of constraints.              
              A standard representation is:
                                            columns
                                            diagonal1
                                            diagonal2
================================================================================================================================================
Step 3 — Diagonal insight:

                      For a cell:   (row, col)
                      
                      the two diagonals can be identified using:                      
                                                                row - col
                                                                row + col                      
                      Specifically:                      
                                      \ diagonal → row - col
                                      / diagonal → row + col
                      
                      This is a very important pattern.
                          For example:   (row, col) = (2, 1)                          
                          gives:                          
                                  row - col = 1
                                  row + col = 3
                          
                          Any other cell with the same row - col lies on the same \ diagonal.                          
                          Any other cell with the same row + col lies on the same / diagonal.
                          
                          So safety becomes approximately:                          
                                                        columnUsed?
                                                        OR
                                                        (row - col) diagonalUsed?
                                                        OR
                                                        (row + col) diagonalUsed?
                          
                          which can be checked in O(1) with sets/boolean arrays.

