L6-level design observation

          There are actually two different optimizations here.
          
          Optimization 1 — State representation:
          
                              Instead of repeatedly scanning the board:   O(N) or O(N²) safety checks
                              
                              we maintain incremental constraint state:                              
                                                                        columns
                                                                        diag1
                                                                        diag2
                              
                              This is a form of incremental state maintenance.
          
          Optimization 2 — Search order:

                                  We place exactly one queen per row.                                  
                                  That immediately eliminates configurations containing:                                  
                                                      two queens in the same row                                  
                                  without ever generating them.
                                  So the representation itself performs pruning.                                  
                                  That's an important architectural principle:                                  
                                            Choose a state representation that makes invalid states impossible or cheap to reject.
